Shit!

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:47.250
Time's up! Good game!

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:51.680
"Mister Barg"
"American Steak"

00:07:57.350 --> 00:07:59.020
Delish!

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:01.390
It's tenderlicious after all!

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:08.230
You think Minato's any better?
Or maybe, because of his accident...

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:12.240
Something like that wouldn't stop him.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:16.490
We know what he's like better than anyone.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:18.740
Yeah.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:19.910
And your little bro?

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:20.910
Hmm?

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:24.250
How's water polo going for him?

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:28.000
Beats me. We haven't talked.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:32.420
He's a fast swimmer, right?
He's cut out for water polo.

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:37.140
Of course he's cut out for it.
He's my brother.

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:40.600
There it is! Momo's subtle bragging!

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:45.350
He'll never beat me, though.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:51.190
I'm number one.
He'll always finish second to me.

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:52.280
Whoa!

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:53.990
More bragging!

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:55.570
Rapid fire!

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:56.780
You making fun?

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:58.530
No, no, no...

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:01.410
We think you're dependable.

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:09.590
"Earlier, I said I had no idea
why this happened to me,

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:14.550
but when I think about it,
I'm not exactly surprised either.

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:19.050
When I was human, I avoided
people as much as possible.

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:21.510
To me, they're arrogant"--

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:35.610
Join you to the music room?

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:38.950
Fine by me.

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:45.120
You're not gonna switch
jerseys, no matter what?

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:49.500
Yeah. I prefer the one I have.

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:52.920
Is it Momo's, by chance?

00:09:55.340 --> 00:10:00.430
Since you're so hung up on it,
I figured it's important.

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:04.310
Yeah. It's my brother's
hand-me-down from fifth grade.

00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:05.560
Fifth grade?!

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:10.650
My mom bought a large one
figuring he'd grow quickly.

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:14.730
I got it the day my parents separated.

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:20.160
Here I thought you were
wearing it short to be stylish.

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:22.030
It's just small.

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:24.910
Why force yourself to wear it?

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:27.500
On that day, he said...

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:28.830
Huh?

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:31.210
Starting today, be my rival!

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:32.590
Rival?

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:37.010
They say having a rival
makes athletes stronger.

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:41.590
Mine is you since you're
the only one fast like me.

00:10:41.590 --> 00:10:45.430
This jersey is proof we're rivals.

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:46.730
Okay!

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:50.980
He's always been better than
others at everything he does...

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:53.940
Always at the center of things...

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:56.740
He was a hero to me.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:11:02.160
As the rival of my hero,
I poured my heart into swimming.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:07.450
I see... That jersey
represents your rivalry.

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:08.710
Wrong.

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:09.830
Huh?

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:13.670
When he went to junior high,
he quit swimming.

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:15.960
Why did you quit?

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:19.670
'Cuz I wanna play water polo instead.

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:23.260
Plus, I found a great rival on the team!

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:25.010
Huh?

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:29.980
I was shocked. I thought I was his rival.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:33.360
That's rough.

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:36.570
Speaking of which, that rival was you.

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:37.820
Me?!

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:40.570
The old you.

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:47.540
Wearing it represents my resolve
to beat him and be his rival again.

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:50.540
So that's how it is.

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:55.090
Which is why you'll never change my mind.

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:04.720
That's it for practice!
Change and let's talk jerseys!

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:05.850
--Okay.
--Right.

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:08.060
I'll be leaving then.

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:12.940
Can you stay and listen?

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:16.190
That's all I'm asking.

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:24.200
Your picks were: Onwards,
challenge, talent, camaraderie.

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:30.160
Once Minato and I say ours,
we'll pick with a show of hands.

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:33.370
You go first.

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:36.500
Um...

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:42.880
I couldn't think of a four-word compound,
but I came up with this:

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:44.800
Surpass yourself!

00:12:47.050 --> 00:12:50.810
Having lost all my memories and talent,

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:56.190
I play water polo so I can get back to
and surpass my old self.

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:05.490
I am my own rival. And I think
that applies to you guys, too.

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:06.740
--Huh?
--Eh?

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:14.290
I feel like we're all playing to move
beyond our past and change ourselves.

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:19.500
Our true rivals are actually
no one but ourselves.

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:22.550
And mine... is this!

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:24.420
"Change"

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:26.720
Change?

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:28.680
Before I explain why, take a look at this.

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:30.180
"Water Polo Memories"

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:30.180
Before I explain why, take a look at this.

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:36.350
After the entrance ceremony last year,
I wandered around a bit.

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:39.190
"Water Polo Club"

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:39.190
I found a club room in really rough shape.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:46.740
After sneaking in, I saw an
album someone left behind.

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:54.450
This guy. He's my dad.

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:56.410
--What?
--Huh?

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:59.460
He used to be the water polo captain.

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:06.130
I forgot all about it
till I saw the photo.

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:13.350
When I was little, we got along and
talked about water polo and stuff.

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:15.980
But after Mom died in an accident,

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:22.650
he found some better paying job
and always came home late.

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:28.450
Even then, he took time out of his
busy schedule to make meals.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:32.370
So, to lighten his load a little bit,

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:37.830
I started eating cup noodles
before he tried to cook.

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:44.630
Looking back, he probably thought
I hated his food or something.

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:48.840
But back then, I never realized that.

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:53.260
Eventually, he cooked less and less...

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:56.520
We spoke less and less...

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:58.770
It got awkward.

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:06.070
I always wanted to change that,
but years went by where I didn't.

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:11.320
These days, we basically avoid
each other, much less talk.

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:20.040
I wanna talk like we used to,
but I never know what to say.

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:22.750
So I revived the club, hoping it'd
give us something to talk about.

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:25.500
"Water Polo Club"

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:25.500
So I revived the club, hoping it'd
give us something to talk about.

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:30.380
The power of love, I guess.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:34.300
Huh? That was about his dad?

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:36.600
"Change," huh?

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:41.190
I want you guys to change, too.

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:42.270
--Huh?
--Eh?

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:46.730
While we've all improved
these past two months,

00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:50.530
we're running too many individual plays.

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:55.160
We won't win without better teamwork.

00:15:55.160 --> 00:16:00.710
It feels like we're a mishmash,
just like our jerseys.

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:06.040
Is that why we're doing this?

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:07.420
Yup.

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:11.590
Mmm. "Change" it is.

00:16:11.590 --> 00:16:12.510
Huh?

00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:18.930
For the jerseys. I'm convinced
after hearing all that.

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:21.390
What about everyone's picks?

00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:25.190
We're all gonna have to change.

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:26.610
Mmm.

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:32.900
What does Amiami think?

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:39.160
Indeed. Without changing,
we can't beat my brother's team.

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:42.410
Yeah! "Change" it is!

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:43.540
--Yeah!
--Right!

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:44.460
So...

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:45.960
Huh?

00:16:45.960 --> 00:16:51.760
I'll change, too,
by wearing our team jersey.

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:53.260
Really?!

00:16:55.720 --> 00:17:00.100
My current one is a little tight.

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:06.690
Now that it's settled...
Ushi! Draw it for us!

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:07.730
Huh?

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:08.860
You can do hand-written
letters for the jersey!

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:11.690
